WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.049
The first images of the newest superhero in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe have hit the

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:08.700
internet — and they look a lot different
than anticipated.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.141
New images from an Atlanta film set show Academy
Award-winning actress Brie Larson actress

00:00:13.141 --> 00:00:18.240
fully suited up as Captain Marvel, aka Air
Force pilot Carol Danvers.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.040
Comic book fans will notice a major difference
between Larson's costume here and the way

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.980
Captain Marvel is usually depicted in comic
books — namely, it's so green.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.450
As Captain Marvel, Carol's colors have largely
always been red, gold, and blue, with her

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.410
Ms. Marvel costume a more revealing black
and yellow.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.450
There is plenty of history in the Captain
Marvel comic books to support the emerald

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.980
suit, however — just not with Carol Danvers
wearing it.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.010
Green is the color most typically associated
with Mar-Vell, the original Captain Marvel,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.610
who is set to be played in the upcoming movie
by Jude Law.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:57.800
Carol received her superpowers due to a disastrous
experience that fused her human DNA with DNA

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.380
of the Kree, a spacefaring alien species of
which Mar-Vell is a member.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.590
Could this be an early version of the suit,
obtained shortly after Carol gets her powers?

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.539
Or is this her new look for the movie, a tribute
to the hero who came before her?

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:14.200
Either way, it's an awesome look — if a
little bit unexpected.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.729
Captain Marvel is expected to soar into theaters
on March 8, 2019.

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:19.820
Thanks for watching!

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.619
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:25.209
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

